      "body": "## Overview\nFix the multi-modal hashing example in `docs/design/prefix_caching.md` so it agrees with the \"only full blocks are cached\" rule (Note 1 on the same page).\n\n## Claims\n- The example now has 4 full blocks, so every block in the list correctly has a hash.\n\n## Validation\n- Before: 8 text tokens + 41 placeholders + 1 end token = 50 tokens. With block size 16, Block 3 has only 2 tokens, so it is not full and must not be hashed. But the example shows a hash for it.\n- After: 8 + 55 + 1 = 64 tokens = 4 full blocks of 16.\n- This matches `get_request_block_hasher()` in `vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py`, which only hashes full blocks.\n\n## Details\nOne-number doc change. I changed the placeholder count instead of removing Block 3's hash, so the rest of the example stays the same.\n\nAI assistance: I used Claude to help find and check this. I reviewed the change myself.",
